body:
Refactored create-event endpoint by creating middleware for each step necessary for the route to complete. This way when an error occurs it is known exactly where the error was thrown and relayed back to the client so the client can retry accordingly. 

Additionally refactored the emailing guests to its own middleware and saved one doc read by hooking into the request body for the guest list rather than getting that data from the doc.

@jesc0bar and @ivancuadra869 I've noticed that both of your user records still have the events field as a map rather than an array. I have yet to deploy this function because I don't know if changing from the events field from map to array will break something in our app. Also Jorge, I do not have the env config set up properly for the nodemailer to create the transport, if you could take care of this on your end that would be sick.
